      "note": "Reviewed verified TSURUWrapper source at https://basescan.org/address/0x75ac62ea5d058a7f88f0c3a5f8f73195277c93da#code, creation receipt/trace, four unauthorized mint traces, all three disposal receipts/traces, and both actors' histories. Earliest trace shows Bueno1155Drop 0xb6740c88659f5991a45bd63b31515f89b9caad57 calling the receiver; it is not immutable trusted ERC1155 0xea4e344fba412f2cd62a8361aa1627133de6c1d5. The supplied id is zero, matching immutable tokenID. These unrelated NFTs cannot redeem the designated backing; accepting their callback violates the wrapper's identity invariant. The seed anchor is the fourth mint. Full paginated Transfer-from-zero history contains 11,681 logs: eight constructor allocations, 11,667 mints of 400 tokens each matched transaction-for-transaction to immutable ERC721 0xc7cd9b38cc75296e9246aabad6fc58ff979eb08e Transfer-to-wrapper logs, the four unauthorized positive mints, and two zero-amount mints. No other positive mint remains unmatched. Full direct history has seven receiver calls: one zero mint and six reverts; nested mint calls are covered by the exhaustive mint-log scan. Both counterfeit recipients dispose their complete minted balance in the three measured sales. Runtime is absent at block 14269613 and its hash matches at deployment and both candidate pre-exploit blocks 14279289/14279785. Direct runtime has no upgrade, delegatecall or selfdestruct path. NFT addresses, id and ratios are immutable/constants; only open/close and ownership can change administratively, and the exploited ERC1155 callback never checks opened or owner. Supply changes affect mint capacity, not the faulty authorization. No later causal-state reset applies; unrelated NFT implementation and disposal routers do not contain the wrapper defect."
